---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { SITE_URL, SITE_NAME, CONTACT, ORGANIZATION } from '../site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Disclaimer"
  description="WorldFreightHub's disclaimer: rates and quotes are indicative estimates not commitments, third-party carrier liability boundaries, and the limits on duty, port and destination cost figures."
  canonical={`${SITE_URL}/disclaimer/`}
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: 'Disclaimer' }]} />
      <h1>Disclaimer</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        WorldFreightHub is a freight information reference, not a carrier,
        forwarder or customs broker. This page sets out, plainly, what the
        figures on this site do and do not mean, and where responsibility for a
        shipment lies.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section container">
    <h2>1. Informational purpose only</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE_NAME} ({SITE_URL}) is operated by{' '}
      <strong>{ORGANIZATION.legalName}</strong>, established in{' '}
      {ORGANIZATION.foundingDate}. The site is an informational and research
      resource for the China–GCC freight corridor. It is{' '}
      <strong>not</strong> a freight forwarder, carrier, customs broker,
      marketplace or legal advisor, and it does not itself carry or clear
      goods.
    </p>
    <p>
      All content on this site — routes, ports, countries, methods, tools and
      directory listings — is provided for general information only. It does
      not constitute an offer to carry goods, a binding quotation, a promise of
      transit time, or professional advice of any kind.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Rates, quotes and transit times are estimates, not commitments</h2>
    <p>
      Every freight rate, transit time, duty, VAT and cost figure on this site
      is an <strong>indicative reference estimate</strong>, not a live price or
      a guaranteed schedule. Figures are labelled HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW
      confidence where data quality permits. A figure shown as a range or a
      single value is a research estimate, not a promise that your shipment
      will cost or take that amount.
    </p>
    <p>
      Freight rates move constantly with fuel prices, seasonal demand, carrier
      capacity, port congestion and geopolitical risk. A rate published today
      may not be available tomorrow, and a rate shown for one lane may not
      apply to a specific shipment with its own weight, volume, commodity and
      delivery terms.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Quotes are not offers and expire</h2>
    <p>
      When you request a quote through the <a href="/get-quote/">get-quote
      form</a>, any rate or transit time a provider returns is{' '}
      <strong>that provider's estimate for your stated shipment details</strong>,
      not a firm offer by {SITE_NAME}. A provider's quote may be subject to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>verification of your cargo's weight, volume, commodity and HS code;</li>
      <li>availability of space on the relevant vessel or route;</li>
      <li>changes in fuel, exchange rates, or port and carrier charges; and</li>
      <li>a validity window, after which the quote lapses.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>The actual rate is only fixed when you receive a written booking
      confirmation from the carrier or forwarder.</strong> Until that written
      confirmation is issued, no figure — on this site or in a quote you
      receive — is a binding price. Always obtain written confirmation of the
      rate, the transit time and the charges included before booking.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Third-party carriers, forwarders and agents</h2>
    <p>
      This site lists freight providers and, through the quote form, routes
      your request to a provider on your selected corridor. The carriage of
      your goods, and any pricing, insurance, cargo loss or damage, delay or
      dispute arising from that carriage, is a matter between{' '}
      <strong>you and that provider</strong> under that provider's own terms
      and conditions. {SITE_NAME} is not a party to that contract.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not act as your agent, and we do not take custody of goods, money
      for freight, or insurance premiums on your behalf. We are not responsible
      for the acts or omissions of any carrier, forwarder, customs broker or
      agent you engage, whether or not they are listed in our directory.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Port, duty and destination charges can change</h2>
    <p>
      Figures for import duty, VAT, port charges, demurrage, detention,
      inspection fees and other destination costs are indicative and can change
      without notice. They depend on factors outside our control, including:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>changes in the destination country's tariff or tax rules;</li>
      <li>the commodity's correct HS code classification;</li>
      <li>customs valuation of the goods; and</li>
      <li>port, terminal and carrier surcharges in force at the time of
      shipment.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Confirm the exact duty, VAT and destination charges for your specific
      commodity and shipment with a licensed customs broker or the destination
      authority before relying on any figure.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Not logistics, legal or trade-compliance advice</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing on this site constitutes logistics, legal, tax, customs or trade
      compliance advice. Information about certifications (such as SABER/SASO
      for Saudi Arabia), import regulations or dangerous-goods rules is
      provided for general awareness and may be incomplete or out of date.
      You are solely responsible for the lawful classification, packing,
      documentation and compliance of your goods, and for obtaining qualified
      professional advice where your shipment requires it.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Accuracy and reliability</h2>
    <p>
      We work to keep information accurate and source-backed, and we publish a
      confidence label with each figure so the reliability is explicit. But we
      do not guarantee that any figure is current at the moment you read it,
      and we do not guarantee that the site is free of errors or omissions.
      Sources change, and data may lag the market.
    </p>
    <p>
      A confidence label of HIGH, MEDIUM or LOW describes how well a figure is
      supported by its source at the time of publication — it is not a
      guarantee of correctness, and a HIGH-confidence figure can still become
      stale as the market moves.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Dangerous goods, certification and commodity-specific rules</h2>
    <p>
      Some commodities — including batteries, chemicals and other regulated or
      dangerous goods — are subject to special classification, packaging,
      labelling and documentation requirements. General information on this
      site about such requirements (for example, SABER/SASO conformity for
      Saudi Arabia, or UN dangerous-goods classification) is provided for
      general awareness only and may be incomplete or out of date for your
      specific product.
    </p>
    <p>
      You are solely responsible for correctly classifying your goods,
      declaring them accurately, and complying with all applicable dangerous-
      goods, certification and customs requirements. Confirm the requirements
      for your exact commodity with a qualified professional before shipping.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Currency and conversion</h2>
    <p>
      Cost figures may be shown in more than one currency. Where a figure is
      converted, the conversion is indicative and based on the exchange rate
      in effect at the time of publication. Actual settlement is in the
      currency and at the rate agreed with the carrier or forwarder.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Force majeure and circumstances beyond control</h2>
    <p>
      Neither we nor any carrier can guarantee a transit time where events
      outside anyone's control — weather, port closures, labour action,
      customs holds, conflict or public health measures — intervene. Any
      transit time on this site is an estimate under normal conditions and is
      subject to such events.
    </p>

    <h2>11. No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The site is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis. To the
      fullest extent permitted by law, {SITE_NAME} and its operator disclaim
      all warranties, express or implied, including warranties of
      merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy and
      non-infringement.
    </p>
    <p>
      We make no warranty that the site will be available at all times, that
      access will be uninterrupted or error-free, or that any defect will be
      corrected. We may modify, suspend or withdraw the site, or any part of
      it, at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, {SITE_NAME} and its operator
      shall not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, special,
      consequential or punitive damages, or for any loss of profits, revenue,
      data or goodwill, arising out of or related to your use of the site or
      your reliance on its information. This includes, without limitation,
      shipping delays, customs penalties, cargo loss or damage, price
      differences and missed commercial opportunities.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Corrections channel</h2>
    <p>
      If you believe any figure or statement on this site is wrong or outdated,
      we want to correct it. Report it through the{' '}
      <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a> or email{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>. We review every
      report and record corrections on the{' '}
      <a href="/data-changelog/">data changelog</a>, so there is a visible
      trail.
    </p>

    <h2>14. Changes to this disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this disclaimer from time to time. The revised version is
      posted on this page with a new "Last updated" date, and material changes
      are announced on the <a href="/data-changelog/">data changelog</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>15. Governing law and severability</h2>
    <p>
      This disclaimer is governed by the laws of the People's Republic of
      China, reflecting the location of the operator,{' '}
      {ORGANIZATION.legalName}, in {ORGANIZATION.address.addressLocality},{' '}
      {ORGANIZATION.address.addressRegion}. If any provision is found invalid
      or unenforceable, it is limited or removed to the minimum extent
      necessary, and the remaining provisions continue in full force and
      effect.
    </p>

    <h2>16. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this disclaimer:{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you are unsure whether a figure on this site applies to your specific
      shipment, ask the carrier or forwarder you are engaging — do not rely on
      the site alone. The quickest way to get a shipment-specific answer is to
      submit the <a href="/get-quote/">get-quote form</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Related policies:{' '}
      <a href="/terms-of-use/">Terms of Use</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/corrections/">Corrections</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: 23 October 2026</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
